skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
' purpose: the CLI surface proveo presents, and the maintainer tooling beside it
' covers: cmd/proveo/main.go
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/main.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/help.go, cmd/proveo/help_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/maintainer_surface_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/env_help.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/running.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/running_test.go
'   the variable registry `help env` renders ... _spec/internal/envreg/env-registry.puml
'
' ── 2026-10-18: `build` VISIBLE, `targets` GONE, `help env` ADDED ──────────
' MEASURED, cmd/proveo/main.go rootCmd(): the root registers version, ls, run,
' schedule, projects, setup, init, update, uninstall, clean, build, deploy,
' test, and the help topic env. main() only executes rootCmd(), so a test can
' render the real root help.
' N9 (option 1): `targets` is deleted with cmd/proveo/targets.go — it had no
' caller. `build` is no longer Hidden, because operator messages tell people to
' run `proveo build <target>`; deploy and test stay Hidden.
' TestRootHelpShowsBuildAndKeepsReleaseToolingHidden pins all three facts.
' N8 (option 1): root help gained a "help topics" section (help.go renderHelp)
' listing `help env`, a cobra help topic rather than a command. `proveo help
' env` draws the operator and maintainer rows of internal/envreg; reported:
' `proveo env` renders the same page because the topic is not runnable.
'
' ── 2026-10-20: END-USER COMMANDS, HARNESS ALIASES, ATTACH ─────────────────
' `build` is Hidden again. mise.toml tasks.build is `go run ./cmd/proveo
' build`, so the command stays registered and stays off root help, beside
' deploy and test. TestRootHelpHidesMaintainerCommands pins that.
' Each manifest target that does not collide with a command is a root
' command: `proveo cursor` is `proveo run cursor`, with the same flags.
' renderHelp lists those under "harnesses", not "commands".
' `proveo attach` is `proveo schedule attach`. With no task, a terminal
' opens a picker of jobs whose tmux session is up and attaches to the
' choice; without a terminal it prints that list and stops. `proveo run`
' with no target prints or picks the same running tasks plus the harness
' list: a running row attaches, a harness row starts. `proveo <harness>`
' with no arguments does that running list only when a task is already up,
' and its last row starts the harness. `--yes`, `--print`, `--ls`,
' `--resume` and `--continue` skip the picker.
'
' ── HELP SPEAKS THE CHOICE PROMPT'S VOCABULARY (2026-09-28) ────────────────
' renderHelp replaces cobra's template on every command with the layout of
' _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml, printed rather than painted:
'   banner + tagline       root only; the tagline IS the root's title
'   title                  bold "<path> — <Short>" on subcommands
'   header                 "usage:" / "aliases:" — label accent, value body
'   Long                   verbatim at the 2-col gutter; an indented block that
'                          opens on `key:` is YAML: key accent, scalar brand,
'                          punctuation body, `# comment` aside
'   ────── commands ──────  heading centered on 72 cols, body style
'   label  text            label accent at col 2, text body at col 24 (or
'                          label+3), wrapped under its column
'   (default …)            aside (italic); skipped when usage already says it
'   hint                   "<path> <command> --help · more on one command"
' Palette = choiceui.styles(): accent ColorAccent bold, body ColorSecondary,
' aside italic. Plain (pipe, NO_COLOR, TERM=dumb) keeps the layout, drops the
' paint, and draws rules in "-", as does PROVEO_GLYPHS=ascii|off.
' cobra's own "help" command is not listed; the hint names --help instead.
'
' ── 2026-10-16/17: `--egress-mode`, `--shell` AND `debug` ARE GONE ─────────
' The Executor: "Nothing, `sbx` handles this. Drop that param"; on stubs:
' "Drop all four" (--egress-mode, --shell, PROVEO_SBX off values, PROVEO_DIND);
' on --shell: "is that `proveo` or `sbx`? if `proveo` retire it"; on the
' maintainer shortcut: "Retire debug too." MEASURED: `proveo run` has neither
' `--egress-mode` nor `--shell`, and cobra answers "unknown flag" for both (no
' stub; the one-day hidden `--egress-mode` refusal is deleted with its test).
' A shell in a run's sandbox is sbx's: `sbx ls`, then `sbx exec -it <sandbox>
' bash`. cmd/proveo-dev/debug.go, its test and `mise run debug` are deleted.
' `--credentials forward|broker` stays and its help names sbx. The
' orchestration packages internal/egress and the runner's docker argv are
' deleted; sidecars (squid, proveo-egress, the Ollama sidecar) are gone, and
' `proveo-dev` lost firehol and `coverage integration`.
'   what decides egress now ... _spec/internal/sbx/policy-baseline.puml
'   the refusal without sbx ... _spec/internal/sbx/sandbox-backend.puml

left to right direction

title Proveo Command Entrypoints

actor "Consumer" as Consumer
actor "Maintainer" as Maintainer

package "Consumer / maintainer entrypoint\ncmd/proveo (static binary)" as Entrypoint {
 component "proveo" as Proveo <<app>>
 component "version · ls · run · schedule · attach · projects · setup · init\nupdate · uninstall · clean\nharness aliases (cursor · …)\nhidden: build · deploy · test · help topic: env" as Commands <<commands>>
 component "run flags\n--credentials · --local-model\n--scope · --print\n--image · --data-dir · --input · --output" as RunFlags <<commands>>
}

package "Installer" as Install {
 component "dist/install.sh\npin release + sha256 verify" as InstallSh <<script>>
 component "goreleaser artifacts\nlinux/darwin × amd64/arm64" as Artifacts <<image>>
}

package "Maintainer binary (not shipped)\ncmd/proveo-dev" as Shims {
 component "proveo-dev coverage · stage-cdn · build-cli\nlint · hooks · ladder · idle · e2e-full" as RunShim <<internal>>
}

package "Maintainer\nmise" as Maint {
 component "mise build|test|deploy" as Mise <<internal>>
 component "proveo build · deploy\ninternal/maintain → internal/imagebuild" as MaintLib <<internal>>
 component "proveo test <target>\ngo test -tags=image ./internal/imagetest" as BuildTest <<internal>>
}

package "Registration" as Reg {
 component "defs/*/harness.manifest\n(embedded in binary)" as Manifests <<config>>
}

package "Orchestration packages\ninternal/" as Orch {
 component "workspace mounts\napp (/app)" as Mounts <<logic>>
 component "run → backend/sandbox\nKit + sbx argv\n--credentials broker|forward" as Egress <<logic>>
 component "provider detect\n(internal/provider)" as Runner <<logic>>
}

package "Runtime" as Runtime {
 component "sbx CLI (+ Docker for images)" as Docker <<runtime>>
 component "proveo/* images" as Images <<image>>
 component "host add-ons\nOllama · CDP · adb" as Sidecars <<runtime>>
 component "workspace + state dir" as Storage <<storage>>
}

Consumer --> Install : first-time install
Install --> Artifacts
Install --> Proveo : places binary on PATH

Consumer --> Proveo : day-to-day
Maintainer --> Proveo : run / --print / list
Maintainer --> Mise : image lifecycle
Mise ..> Shims : one command per task

Proveo --> Commands
Commands --> RunFlags
Proveo --> Manifests : enumerate targets
Proveo --> Orch : compose plan
Orch --> Docker
Orch --> Images
Orch --> Sidecars
Orch --> Storage

RunShim ..> Proveo : e2e-full · ladder · idle → proveo run <target>
Mise ..> BuildTest
Mise ..> MaintLib
Mise ..> Proveo : run/list when needed
MaintLib --> Images : buildx --load / --push
BuildTest ..> Images : image contract suites

note right of Proveo
**Product CLI is Go only.**
No installed bash lib/*.sh runners.
""PROVEO_DEFS_DIR"" overrides embeds for dev.

**One binary composed of packages**, and the
composition is the point: ""internal/run"" resolves the
run, ""internal/backend/sandbox"" renders the Kit and the
sbx argv, ""internal/provider"" detects which vendor a
run is talking to. (Until 2026-10-16 ""internal/runner""
built a docker-run argv and ""internal/egress"" a docker
topology; both are deleted.) That logic was previously triplicated
across the consumer CLI, ""lib/runners\.sh"" and every
per-def ""run\.sh"" — three copies that drifted. The last
""run\.sh"" shims went in host-shell-to-go P4.

Shipped as a single checksummed static binary
(""\.goreleaser\.yaml"", ""dist/install\.sh""), which is what
lets a consumer run a harness without a source checkout.
end note

note bottom of Artifacts
**The version string is stamped in at link time, never read at runtime.**
The variable's literal in ""main\.go"" is ""dev"" and the real value arrives
from the linker (""-ldflags -X main\.version=<v>""): a dev install
(""mise run build-cli"") stamps ""dev@<git-short-sha>"", so a bug report
names the commit it came from, while a release stamps the semver tag.
A binary built outside either path keeps the literal and honestly
reports ""dev"" rather than claiming a release it is not.
end note

note bottom of Commands
**The tagline is printed once, which is why cobra's ""Short"" is left empty
on the root command.** ""ui\.WriteBrandBanner"" already renders it dimmed
under the banner from the root help hook, so filling ""Short"" in as well
would print the same line twice on ""proveo --help"".

**A message about the absence of results is not a result.**
""proveo projects"" with nothing to list writes its note to stderr and
leaves stdout empty, so a scripted caller counting rows sees zero rows
instead of one line of prose it would have to recognise and discard.
end note

note bottom of Commands
**The command list is the whole consumer surface.** cobra's
default ""completion"" command is disabled rather than
inherited: a shell-completion generator is maintainer
plumbing, and every command shown here is something a
consumer is meant to run.
end note

note right of RunFlags
""proveo run <target>"" applies to every
harness with a manifest (claudecode*,
opencode, cursor, codex, hermes). Every run goes
to an sbx sandbox with its own daemon (hermes:
""daemon: false""); a host without sbx refuses
the run. No manifest declares ""docker:"" (F10).
end note

note bottom of Egress
sbx's own policy decides egress; proveo adds
only add-on reach to the Kit. ""--local-model""
uses the host's Ollama (not for cursor). Run
artifacts under the host state dir.
end note

@enduml
